        "path": "_m/9/r/9/6/collier-memorial-state-park-wp/wood-burning-locomotive-collie.jpg",
        "filename": "Wood Burning Locomotive Collier Memorial State Park.jpg",
        "caption": "Vital statistics: Gauege 4 feet 8 1/2 inches; Fuel wood or soft coal; boiler diameter 38 inches; Wheel base 72 inches; cylinders 13 inches by 30 inches; diameter of drivers 37 inches; tank capacity 800 gallons; smoke stack diamond; steam pressure 130 pounds; weight 45,000 pounds; built 1884.\nThis locomotive was nicknamed “GOP” “Get Out and Push” because it derailed quite iften. The locomotive was designed to haul 70 gross tons of car and cargo up a 4% grade. This engine was used in the California redwoods and around Mt Shasta from 1890.",
        "alt": "Vital statistics: Gauege 4 feet 8 1/2 inches; Fuel wood or soft coal; boiler diameter 38 inches; Wheel base 72 inches; cylinders 13 inches by 30 inches; diameter of drivers 37 inches; tank capacity 800 gallons; smoke stack diamond; steam pressure 130 pounds; weight 45,000 pounds; built 1884.\nThis locomotive was nicknamed “GOP” “Get Out and Push” because it derailed quite iften. The locomotive was designed to haul 70 gross tons of car and cargo up a 4% grade. This engine was used in the California redwoods and around Mt Shasta from 1890.",
